# Changelog

As short as possible. User-facing changes only.

- One line per change, saying what a user can now do or what behaves differently.
- Keep a Changelog headings (Added / Changed / Fixed / Removed), newest release first.
- Bump `version` in `package.json` alongside a new release heading.

Leave out entirely — no entry, not even a short one:

- build, test, CI, tooling, dependency and refactor work
- file, function or module names
- why the change was made, or how it was implemented

```markdown
<!-- BAD: not user-facing -->
### Build and test
- `selftest` and `inttest` run in headless Chrome against the real bundle.

<!-- BAD: implementation detail and reasoning -->
- Corners weld through a shared-vertex map, so adjacent quads sample the same edge
  instead of each interpolating their own.

<!-- GOOD -->
### Added
- Curved mark edges, two Bézier handles per side.

### Fixed
- Atlas packing no longer overlaps rotated slices.
```
